{{Top|notoc=1}}
{{Quote|I can't see a thing in this helmet.|[[Luke Skywalker]]|<ref name="Episode 4">{{Film|IV}}</ref>}}
[[File:HelmetsCompiled-SWGoH.png|300px|thumb|right|Various helmets worn throughout [[the galaxy]]]]
A '''helmet''' was a component of [[armor]] worn on an individual's head. The [[Mandalorian super commando]]s sometimes decorated their helmets with horns.<ref name="Mandalorian Super Commando">{{Databank|mandalorian-super-commando|Mandalorian Super Commando}}</ref> [[Clone trooper]]s wore helmets as part of their [[Clone trooper armor|armor]], and occasionally referred to them as '''sun bonnets'''.<ref name="Rookies">{{TCW|Rookies (episode)}}</ref> Members of the [[104th Battalion]]<ref name="Rising Malevolence Ep Guide">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/rising-malevolence-episode-guide|text="Rising Malevolence" Episode Guide &#124; The Clone Wars}}</ref> led by the [[Jedi General]] [[Plo Koon]]<ref name="Rising Malevolence">{{TCW|Rising Malevolence|Rising ''Malevolence''}}</ref> painted stylized wolf muzzles painted on their helmets.<ref name="Rising Malevolence Ep Guide" /> The [[Sith trooper]]s of the [[Final Order]] wore [[Color|red]] helmets made out of [[gammaplast]].
<ref name="TROS VD">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref>

[[Wookiee]] helmets contained a crest of an ancient [[Star|sun]] symbol, and Wookiee [[hair]] could be threaded through its perforated flange.<ref name="CVD">''[[Star Wars: The Complete Visual Dictionary, New Edition]]''</ref>

Helmets were standard equipment in [[grav-ball]] and often got dirty.<ref name="Edge">''[[Servants of the Empire: Edge of the Galaxy]]''</ref>

[[Z'Vk'Thkrkza|Aunt Z]] had a shelf of [[flight helmet]]s from across several decades in her [[Aunt Z's Tavern|tavern]], including [[Mandalorian armor|Mandalorian]], clone trooper, [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]], and [[rebel pilot]].<ref name="Bucket's">{{SW|url=news/buckets-list-extra-the-high-tower-star-wars-resistance|text=Bucket's List Extra: 9 Fun Facts from "The High Tower" - ''Star Wars Resistance''|date=2018-10-29|quote=Aunt Z has a shelf of pilot helmets from across the decades, including Mandalorian, Imperial, clone, and rebel pilot.}}</ref>

{{Clothes-stub}}

